NAME
    cd - change the working directory

SYNOPSIS
    cd [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Makes path the current directory. The path may be absolute (/BIN),
    relative (T/SUB), or use . and .. (every directory's own first two
    entries); cd / is the root. The prompt shows the new path. cd with
    no path changes nothing. Names are case-sensitive. Errors: "not
    found", "not a directory" (the current directory stays as it was).
    cd is a shell built-in.

LIMITS
    The path the prompt and pwd show is kept in 64 bytes.

EXAMPLES
    cd /BIN
    cd ..
    cd /MAN

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: the drive-1 mount (cd /d1).
    The command is the Y1/OS shell's own (os/y1os.c); the page is
    ported from P8X os/man/cd 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    pwd, dir, mkdir, ls
